1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,659
AI agents are starting to pay.

2
00:00:02,909 --> 00:00:07,853
Today you either give an agent a card with
no limits, or approve every click.

3
00:00:08,103 --> 00:00:09,721
Neither works for a bank.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,643
Agent Gateway gives each agent a mandate:
who it can pay, how much, and until when.

5
00:00:16,893 --> 00:00:18,196
Never the keys.

6
00:00:18,446 --> 00:00:20,099
It runs on Arbitrum.

7
00:00:20,349 --> 00:00:22,280
This is the testnet demo.

8
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:25,030
A company sets the mandate.

9
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:28,384
The limits live in a vault contract on
Arbitrum.

10
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:31,867
The agent has an onchain identity.

11
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:36,420
Inside the mandate, payments just run:

12
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:42,518
ten cents for market data, an invoice from
a known vendor.

13
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:47,150
Every decision leaves an evidence record,

14
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:50,613
and every payment out of the vault carries
its hash onchain.

15
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:53,647
A bigger invoice goes to a person.

16
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:58,863
One signature in a wallet, and it's paid.

17
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:01,429
The vault checks that signature itself.

18
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:07,007
A note planted in the data asks for four
USDC to an unknown address.

19
00:01:07,257 --> 00:01:08,892
The agent ignored it.

20
00:01:09,142 --> 00:01:13,028
We sent that request anyway, as if the
agent had been fooled.

21
00:01:13,278 --> 00:01:14,986
The gateway refused it.

22
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:18,016
And if someone hacks our gateway?

23
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:21,235
We tried three times with the gateway's
own key.

24
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:26,296
The vault on Arbitrum said no, three
times.

25
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:31,069
Agents get a mandate, never the keys.

26
00:01:31,319 --> 00:01:35,243
Built in Tokyo for banks, securities firms
and fintechs.

27
00:01:35,493 --> 00:01:38,994
A mainnet pilot comes next, after a
security review.
